      "id": "technical-report-dynamic-web",
      "area": "writing",
      "collection": "writing-technical",
      "kind": "document",
      "title": "Securing a Dynamic Website · Technical Report Outline",
      "date": "2009-03-16",
      "excerpt": "Purpose, restrictions, and a two-section outline covering static and dynamic web services.",
      "body": "<p><strong>Shawn Stark · March 16, 2009</strong></p><h3>Purpose and scope</h3><p>This paper is intended to serve as documented theory, purpose and rationale for dynamic multi-user, data and application services from the perspective of client/server-side web application. The approach outlined directly applies to well-documented performance, site usage, security, convenience, ease of use, portability, distributed capability, and specifically the security that is required thereof. This is a preliminary paper subject to additions and modifications; it is in no way a primer for the use of said application, or a how to manual. All final disclaimers and rights will be found in the published version. This preliminary paper is not to be viewed, distributed, copied in whole or part; without the express authorization of the author, creative director, analyst, programmer and executive official: Shawn Nicholas Stark. Those whom are authorized must confide they will not share the structure and general ideas expressed within, in such a way that would jeopardize the production or the proceeds that are related in any way to the information contained herein prior to reading any further.</p><h3>Technical report outline</h3><h4>Section 1 · Static service</h4><ul><li>Introduction</li><li>Login &amp; User Verification</li><li>Access Records</li><li>Directory Security</li><li>Main Entry Point</li><li>Session and User data</li><li>Dissemination &amp; loading</li><li>Permissions &amp; Subscriptions</li><li>Global and Group files</li><li>SysUsr Special Group</li><li>Unrecorded Files/Backdoor1</li><li>Possible Distributed User Folders</li><li>Other Thoughts and Publication Links</li><li>Relation To Remaining Sections</li></ul><h4>Section 2 · Dynamo service</h4><ul><li>Introduction</li><li>Keys and Loader Registration</li><li>Base Loading System</li><li>Running Commands</li><li>Loading Libraries</li><li>Loading Applications</li><li>Client Side debugging</li><li>Application Template</li><li>Handling all of this Server Side</li></ul>",
      "files": [],
